+# Focused review corrections
+
+- Adopter verification now enforces the SDK 11 policy and the exact selected 11.0 patch for both shared frameworks. Quality Gate 4a chooses only a stable ASP.NET Core 11.0 runtime and reports an explicit error if none exists. Positive and negative SDK/framework and actual gate-shell fixtures distinguish these cases.
+- Generated submit entry is marshaled to the renderer, and pre-dispatch host/auth continuations preserve it. A field-change revision invalidates validation that awaited an older model value. Held asynchronous hidden/blocked host callbacks and a changed-field/released-admission/fresh-retry regression pass alongside the six existing validation controls. Both snapshots match.
+- Account observations withdraw the prior identity while pending, protect synchronous provider invocation as well as asynchronous completion, retain revision/disposal guards, and observe unexpected failures through DispatchExceptionAsync. Pending-notification, stale initial-read, synchronous-failure, stale notification, disposal and fatal-routing regressions use actual completion tasks.
+- The two best-effort shell focus calls now handle ObjectDisposedException from a cached module released during focus. Held-focus teardown tests confirm disposal is contained and unrelated InvalidOperationException still propagates.
+- Current Memories install/runtime/remediation text and its sandbox command, plus the four requested FrontComposer operational/framework documents, now match .NET 11. Dated proof and explicit external SDK 10.0.302/10.0.404 compatibility instructions remain.
+
+Verification is deliberately narrow: 27 adopter tests, 68 emitter tests and 24 generated-form/account/focus cases pass (119 total). SourceTools.Tests and Shell.Tests build individually in Debug/source mode with warnings as errors. Exact commands and report hashes are in review-fixes-results.json; XML stays in /tmp/tenants-net11-repair-ng54_u4z/. Both owning git diff --check commands pass. Full verification is left to the parent as requested.
